   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to waiving the residency\nrequirement for certain assistant district attorney positions within Saratoga\nCounty",
    "basePrintNo": "S8634",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8634-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8634\n\nSPONSOR: TEDISCO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to waiving the\nresidency requirement for certain assistant district attorney positions\nwithin Saratoga County\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nPermits residents outside of Saratoga county to hold the position of\nassistant district attorney in Saratoga County.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one adds subdivision 74 to section 3 of the public officers law\nallowing residents of counties which adjoin Saratoga County to serve as\ndistrict attorneys in Saratoga County. This provision does not apply to\nthe position of chief assistant district attorney.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill has been introduced at the request of the Saratoga County\nDistrict Attorney's Office. This legislation will allow Saratoga County\nto expand its pool of eligible applicants and be able to hire qualified\nindividuals from adjoining counties to hold the position of assistant\ndistrict attorney in Saratoga County. Similar authorizations have been\nprovided to multiple counties across NYS.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
